      {
        "detail": "R5: Resuming an eligible saved call renews inherited source-bearing taskStatus strings. VoiceSessionController.resumeCall (152-169) copies latest.taskStatus into a new UUID with startedAtMs=now, then MainActivity (173-175) calls linkConversation, which clears the copied transcript while retaining taskStatus (VoiceSessionController 174-176). VoiceCallStore.save/sanitize (31-35,43-67) only finds prior by the new call ID and dates derived title/task text from that new startedAtMs; it does not preserve inherited source lineage. Given an accepted persisted/legacy task string \"Opened Amber Notebook\" captured at t0, resume at day89 and link the conversation; at t0+90 days the original call expires but the new call retains the copied task text until day179, including after reopen. Current accepted-action Runtime generally writes content-free tool names, so the source-bearing persisted/legacy task precondition is explicit; the public store/codec and privacy contract nevertheless accept and cover arbitrary task strings. Content-free identity/outcome preservation can remain allowed. Keep derived-source provenance separate from session start across new-ID resume and the later transcript-clearing checkpoint, or fail closed for unprovenanced inherited freeform tasks. Repair can live in allowed VoiceCallStore without editing frozen controller/activity. Add a boundary regression that saves eligible prose tasks, follows resume+link, advances to original expiry, and reopens. Evidence: privacy-review-4-retention-probe.json is an exact source-level lifecycle model, not a Kotlin run.",
