      {
        "detail": "R6: recordSourceInferencePrompt (lines 33-37) computes sources.minOfOrNull { minOf(it.capturedAtMs, sourceTimestamp()) } before validation. It then passes only that derived clock and source text strings to wrap/Privacy.placeholder, losing each source\u2019s original clock. With clock/sourceTimestamp=1000 and a benign FullSource capturedAtMs=1001 (future) or Long.MAX_VALUE (overflowing expiry), the method produces captured=1000 and persists/binds the payload, even though Privacy.eligible rejects the original capture time. The supplied voice FullSource API must reject every missing/future/overflow/expired original clock before choosing the oldest eligible clock; an earlier history timestamp is not proof of that source\u2019s capture provenance. This violates the explicit fail-closed invalid-clock requirement. The reduced clock is conservative for age but still masks invalid source provenance. The current full-source test covers valid epoch timestamps and secret text, not invalid clocks. Evidence: privacy-review-4-clock-probe.json evaluates the exact source arithmetic; no Kotlin execution claimed.",
